'''Dandicus Dancifer''', more commonly known as '''Dandy''', is the titular [[Toon]] and mascot of [[Dandy's World]]. He acts as a shopkeeper for Toons, Trinkets, and [[Gamepasses]], appears between [[Floors]] as an [[Item]] vendor, and is a developer-exclusive character, though playable in [[Roleplay Mode]].

==Appearance==
<tabber>
|-|Default=
Dandy is a short humanoid flower Toon. His most defining features are his petals, having six that are individually red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple, in a clockwise order, with red being at the very top of his head. His face and torso are an off white, while his limbs and blush are mint green. When feeling major negative emotions, he has red dots in his eyes, much like [[Twisteds]].
|-|Christmas=
Dandy's Christmas [[Skin]] gives him a forest green sweater with yellow buttons, as well as patterned edges on the sleeves and decorated with embroidered patterns in the shape of loops, both of which being a dark red. He also wears a plain white undershirt, red pants with light red stripes, and dark red boots with white furred cuffs.
|-|Easter=
Dandy's Easter [[Skin]] gives him a white bunny-ear headband with pastel pink inner ears, and white gloves with dark pink stitching. He has a dark pink sleeveless button-up vest with triangular edges that meet in the middle and a white collar. Additionally, he wears a bubblegum pink pair of shorts with pastel pink stripes and a white bunny tail.
|-|Halloween=
Dandy's Halloween [[Skin]] gives him an orange headband with dark purple bat wings that have black membranes. He wears a dark purple tailcoat along with similarly colored bat wings on his back. He also has orange boot-cut pants with light yellow stripes, black pumps, and white socks.
</tabber>

==Personality==
At first glance, Dandy seems to be a kind, responsible and bright [[Toon]], but also suspicious and harboring darker secrets. Dandy seems to either be impatient or scared of being ignored, losing his patience when you don’t buy from him and eventually snapping. Despite Dandy being stated to not be fully evil, it has been implied that he has done questionable things with the [[Ichor]] Operation.

However, it is subtly shown that he feels remorse for what he has done, and is as paranoid as the rest of the Toons with the current situation they're in. Dandy stays silent and says nothing other than "{{Text|...}}" when you buy {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, which implies he may feel remorse for his {{CI|Twisted Dandy}}[[Twisted Dandy|Twisted counterpart]] reveal. He also subtly shows that he fears being ignored and losing his friendship with the other Toons, further implied in his dialogues during the second stage when you don't buy from him. Yet, he tries to cover most of it up by acting like nothing happened after encountering his Twisted counterpart, trying to keep up his cheerful act. This could be a sign of him hiding his twisted form as an evidence.

Despite this, Dandy is genuinely fond of some Toons, namely his pet rock {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and likely Astro. This is visible in some of Astro and Pebble's dialogue, as well as an official statement that Dandy wouldn't be a bad owner to Pebble and that Dandy and Astro's relationship is not toxic. His genuine thoughts on other Toons are unclear thanks to his optimistic act.

As of the Queens of Mischief music video, there is now further evidence of good behavior that assists in balancing out the bad behavior. While watching the titular band perform, Dandy is genuinely enjoying their performance with a much happier expression than everyone else in the audience, who in turn all don't mind his presence.

Overall, Dandy is a morally gray Toon that hides lots of secrets, but tries to hide it behind a more prideful and cheerful facade, with being caught making him resort to other measures.

==Gameplay==
Dandy is a shopkeeper NPC who helps the [[Toons]] by selling [[Items]] to help them descend to the next [[floor]]. He always appears on even-numbered floors before the elevator opens and sells 3 random Items. Some Items can only be obtained through his shop while some can also appear on floors. However, if the Toons don't buy his items, he starts to get frustrated and will have a chance turn into his {{CI|Twisted Dandy}}[[Twisted Dandy|Twisted form]] after being ignored 3 times, being near guaranteed on the 4th time you ignore him. After his Twisted form appears, he will go back to normal.

Dandy can also be seen in the lobby. When interacted with, his shop opens. In his shop, he sells Toons and [[Trinkets]] for [[Ichor]]. There is also an option in his shop for [[Gamepasses]], which can be bought with Robux.

